      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: require exact claims for direct cloud cleanup",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- require canonical lease IDs before DigitalOcean, Linode, Vultr, or Scaleway resources enter Crabbox inventory\n- require exact provider/account-or-project/resource-bound local claims before reuse, stop, status-touch, or cleanup\n- keep claimless canonical resources read-only until explicit `--reclaim` adoption; never synthesize destructive ownership from remote tags\n- preserve interrupted-create recovery while validating exact provider identity\n- restrict key-only Scaleway and Vultr recovery claims to identityless key cleanup; they cannot authorize live server deletion\n- keep read-only resolve paths from writing claims\n- document the ownership boundary in provider and stop documentation\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/811\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent candidate: `6e12ac99bfbe4020d779e96e5046495a919c7233`.\n\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/vultr ./internal/providers/scaleway -count=1`\n- `go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/vultr ./internal/providers/scaleway`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- Full branch autoreview clean; focused key-only Vultr recovery autoreview clean (0.86).\n- All inline review findings are fixed, answered, and resolved.\n\n## Provider-live proof\n\n- DigitalOcean at `9d074c70`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_41ac9aa551b8`.\n- Linode at `9d074c70`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_fed152b988e2`.\n- Scaleway at `ee82a6fb`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_f91178ad1c09`.\n- Vultr: pending because no authenticated API credential is available after targeted environment and approved 1Password lookup.\n\nThe later commits affect only provider-neutral rebase context and key-only Vultr recovery rejection; they do not weaken the proven DigitalOcean, Linode, or Scaleway paths.\n\nKeep this PR unmerged until exact-head Vultr create/use/status-touch/stop/empty-inventory proof passes, or that provider-specific gate is explicitly waived.\n\n## Compatibility decision\n\nAccepted fail-closed behavior: claimless, provider-identity-mismatched, or recovery-ambiguous resources remain inspectable but cannot be touched or deleted until explicit reclaim establishes an exact claim.\n",
